A. Commit message:
KVM: nVMX: Defer SVI update to vmcs01 on EOI when L2 is active w/o VID

B. Change summary:
This patch defers the update of GUEST_INTERRUPT_STATUS.SVI in vmcs01 until L1 is active, ensuring that vISR tracking remains accurate when L2 is active without Virtual Interrupt Delivery (VID). This prevents L1 interrupts from being incorrectly blocked due to a stale SVI value. Additionally, it includes necessary changes to handle APIC base setting and address canonical checks.

C. Compatibility Risk:
Medium: Code diff will be applied and a pull request will be sent to the developer to merge, but there are no indirect changes expected to be done in other parts of the system.

